The recency check keys on commit-count distance, and this branch's own two
commits pushed the recorded generation point to 16 commits ago, one past
the 15-commit window. Not a content change in the doc's subject matter.

Recorded because the mitigation is not the obvious one: all five
verify-generated --check gates were pre-flighted GREEN before the first
push. Pre-flighting is necessary but NOT sufficient — any commit added
after the pre-flight (here, the manifest fix; more usually auto-pr's own
rebase onto a moved dev) shifts the window underneath it. Re-check after
the last commit, not before the first.

